{
  "title": "Course Management, Enrollment, and Learner Progress System Documentation",
  "functional_domain": "Learning Management System (LMS) Core Features",
  "description": "This report synthesizes documentation for a merged software cluster, providing a comprehensive overview of the Course Management, Enrollment, and Learner Progress System. It integrates insights from foundational documentation with additional components, highlighting the full scope of functionality for defining courses, managing content, handling user enrollment, tracking learner progress, and providing administrative oversight.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "1. Course Definition and Content Management",
      "content": "This section details the processes and components involved in defining courses, structuring their content, and managing various types of learning materials.",
      "sub_sections": [
        {
          "title": "1.1 Course Creation and Metadata",
          "content": "Course metadata, including title, course code, abstract, description, target groups, and learning goals, is primarily managed through the `Admin::CourseForm` (app/forms/admin/course_form.rb). This form also handles critical attributes such as `status`, `lang`, `channel_id`, and various feature flags like `roa_enabled`, `cop_enabled`, `pinboard_enabled`, and `invite_only`. Course visuals and stage visuals are managed via uploads, processed by the `Course::Visual::Store` operation (app/operations/course/visual/store.rb), which facilitates S3 interactions for images and teaser videos, including subtitles. Course classifiers are also managed through this form, with built-in validation for format and uniqueness."
        },
        {
          "title": "1.2 Course Structure (Sections)",
          "content": "Course sections, which organize content, are managed by the `SectionsController` (app/controllers/sections_controller.rb). Teachers can perform CRUD operations (create, update, destroy) and reorder sections. The controller interacts with the `Xikolo::Course::Section` microservice client to persist these changes. For courses not yet migrated to a new content tree, a `load_raw_sections` method is used to load sections and their items. The frontend UI (app/assets/teacher/sections/sections.js) provides functionality to toggle UUIDs and manage delete restrictions. Implicit tags for pinboards are automatically created when a section is saved. The `SectionPresenter` (app/presenters/section_presenter.rb) is used to display section details, including item availability and alternative sections."
        },
        {
          "title": "1.3 Content Item Management",
          "content": "Content items within sections are managed by the `ItemsController` (app/controllers/items_controller.rb), supporting diverse content types including `video`, `rich_text`, `quiz`, and `lti_exercise`.\n\n*   **Creation**: The `Item::Create` operation (app/operations/item/create.rb) orchestrates the creation of an item and its associated content resource, ensuring content validity, setting `content_id` and `section_id`, and creating implicit pinboard tags.\n*   **Rich Text**: `Course::Richtext` content is processed by `Course::Richtext::Store` (app/operations/course/richtext/store.rb), which handles text processing, S3 uploads for embedded files, and manages file references. Frontend logic (`handleRichTextType` in app/assets/teacher/items/rich-text.ts) dynamically adjusts the item creation/edit form for rich text content.\n*   **Video**: Video items utilize `Video::Video` and `Video::Store` (app/operations/course/visual/store.rb) for managing video streams, subtitles, slides, and reading materials.\n*   **Quiz**: Quiz items interact with `Xikolo::Quiz::Quiz` and its associated question types.\n*   **LTI Exercise**: LTI exercises leverage `Lti::Exercise` and `Lti::Provider`.\n\nThe `ItemsController` also facilitates moving items within or between sections, accommodating both legacy and tree-based course structures. Item deletion involves removing the item via the `course_api` and, for most content types, destroying the associated content resource."
        },
        {
          "title": "1.4 Documents",
          "content": "Course documents are managed by `Course::DocumentsController` (app/controllers/course/documents_controller.rb) and `DocumentHelper` (app/helpers/document_helper.rb). These components interact with the `course_api` to list, show, create, update, and delete documents and their localizations. File uploads for documents are handled via `FileUpload` with a `course_document` purpose."
        },
        {
          "title": "1.5 Poll Management",
          "content": "The system includes administrative capabilities for managing interactive elements. `Admin::PollOptionsController` (Admin::PollOptionsController) is responsible for managing the options available for polls, suggesting a configurable system for integrating polling features within courses or as standalone engagement tools."
        },
        {
          "title": "1.6 Course Context and Access Control",
          "content": "`CourseContextHelper` (app/helpers/course_context_helper.rb) and `ItemContextHelper` (app/helpers/item_context_helper.rb) provide shared logic for course and item-related pages. The `inside_course` method sets a course-specific layout and enforces `check_course_eligibility` to ensure users have appropriate permissions or enrollment status. Similarly, `inside_item` ensures the item belongs to the course and loads necessary presenters."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "2. Enrollment Lifecycle Management",
      "content": "This section covers the entire lifecycle of user enrollment in courses, from initial registration to unenrollment and reactivation, including administrative policies and statistics.",
      "sub_sections": [
        {
          "title": "2.1 Enrollment and Unenrollment",
          "content": "User enrollment is managed by the `Course::EnrollmentsController` (app/controllers/course/enrollments_controller.rb). The `create` action attempts to enroll a user via a `POST` request to `course_api.rel(:enrollments)`, handling various error scenarios like `access_restricted` or `prerequisites_unfulfilled`. Users already enrolled are redirected to the course resume path. The `destroy` action allows unenrollment via a `DELETE` request to the enrollment's `self` relation via the `course_api`."
        },
        {
          "title": "2.2 Course Launch and Reactivation",
          "content": "The `Course::LaunchController` (app/controllers/course/launch_controller.rb) handles initial course access, redirecting unauthenticated users to login or authenticated users to enrollment, storing the intended course location in the session. `Course::FreeReactivationsController` (app/controllers/course/free_reactivations_controller.rb) enables users to reactivate courses under specific conditions, interacting with the `course_api` to check prerequisites and create new reactivations. The platform's `course_reactivation` feature flipper and course configuration determine if reactivation is enabled. Presenters like `CourseInfoPresenter` (app/presenters/course_info_presenter.rb) and `CourseLargePreviewPresenter` (app/presenters/course_large_preview_presenter.rb) expose logic for checking course reactivation eligibility."
        },
        {
          "title": "2.3 Enrollment Policies and Statistics",
          "content": "Administrative control over enrollment rules is facilitated by `Course::EnrollmentPolicyForm` (Course::EnrollmentPolicyForm), allowing for the definition and management of enrollment policies. `Course::EnrollmentStatistics` (Course::EnrollmentStatistics) provides aggregated data and insights into enrollment trends and user participation, crucial for reporting and course management."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "3. Learner Progress and Engagement",
      "content": "This section details how learner progress is tracked, displayed, and how users navigate and engage with course content, including achievements and dashboard integrations.",
      "sub_sections": [
        {
          "title": "3.1 Progress Tracking and Visualization",
          "content": "The `Course::ProgressController` (app/controllers/course/progress_controller.rb) displays a user's progress, fetching data from `course_api.rel(:progresses)` for the current user or a specified user (with teaching permissions). The `ProgressHelper` (app/helpers/progress_helper.rb) provides the `calc_progress` method to compute percentage progress. Visual representation of progress is enhanced by `Course::CircularProgress` (Course::CircularProgress), likely a UI component for displaying progress in a user-friendly circular format."
        },
        {
          "title": "3.2 Syllabus and Content Access",
          "content": "The `Course::SyllabusController` (app/controllers/course/syllabus_controller.rb) provides an overview of course content, including a progress summary, and handles open mode access for previewable items. The `ItemPresenter` (app/presenters/item_presenter.rb) is central for displaying individual items, providing status (locked, visited, active), type labels, and time effort. It also determines item previewability based on `open_mode` and content type (currently restricted to video). The `ItemContextHelper` (app/helpers/item_context_helper.rb) includes `create_visit!` to record user visits to items, excluding quizzes or masquerading sessions."
        },
        {
          "title": "3.3 Certificates and Achievements",
          "content": "`DocumentsPresenter` (app/presenters/documents_presenter.rb) is responsible for presenting available certificates (Confirmation of Participation, Record of Achievement, Certificate, Transcript of Records) and open badges. It checks for template existence and user eligibility (e.g., passing proctoring for certificates) based on enrollment and course configuration."
        },
        {
          "title": "3.4 Course Navigation",
          "content": "`CourseNav` (app/presenters/course_nav.rb) defines the primary navigation items for learners (sections, discussions, progress, certificates, documents). `CourseTeacherNav` (app/presenters/course_teacher_nav.rb) provides navigation for teachers (dashboards, content management, settings, enrollments, grading)."
        },
        {
          "title": "3.5 Dashboard and Calendar Integration",
          "content": "The system supports dashboard functionalities and integrations. `Dashboard::IcalFeed` (Dashboard::IcalFeed) enables the generation of iCal feeds, allowing users to integrate course schedules, deadlines, and events into their personal calendars, enhancing overall course management and engagement."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
